{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-alg-002-kaplansky-s-conjectures-86dd5663-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T15:37:58Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-alg-002-kaplansky-s-conjectures-86dd5663-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-alg-002-kaplansky-s-conjectures-86dd5663-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-alg-002-kaplansky-s-conjectures-86dd5663-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/ALG-002"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "A set of conjectures about group rings: (1) Zero divisor conjecture: If $G$ is a torsion-free group and $K$ is a field, then $K[G]$ has no zero divisors. (2) Idempotent conjecture: The only idempotents in $K[G]$ are 0 and 1. (3) Unit conjecture: The only units in $\\mathbb{Z}[G]$ are of the form $\\pm g$ for $g \\in G$."}, "statement_sha256": "ffc94b0c061eb7a2807d46a4a48bd948960ec15782d7e47b11857334083fd602"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-alg-002-kaplansky-s-conjectures-86dd5663-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/ALG-002"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha256": "eb2386678ad21f35b757a02c3292b04b85ccde46a37a711e3399b1b5640cf9ad", "problem_id": "problem:um-alg-002-kaplansky